That is, of course, not what I said; fortunately you did quote what I
_actually_ said above, so I don't have to waste time re-quoting it.

# of kills, XP, HP, Pw, gold, # of items -- all of these are things that
could conceivably be rewarded with score points.  However, an attempt to
reward high values of any of these is rendered immediately worthless by
farming in the current system..

> No wonder you dislike farming so much! So extinctionists
> rock, but lowest kills, didn't kill uniques, ascended with 80 maxHP,
> all that stuff is "alternate victory conditions" that you don't take
> seriously, right?

Any of these are _also_ criteria that might be worth including as a
score.  It would be nice if the scoring system were able to
detect/identify/utilize ALL criteria, rather than just an isolated few.

(<nitpick> 'ascended with 80 maxHP' isn't actually so good, because you
only have to hang out next to Death for awhile to arrange for that; the
game would need to track the most HP you _ever_ had, not just what you
had at time-of-ascension.  </nitpick>  This is easily doable, though.)

